# apocalypse-boot2.vrs: apocalypse D28 (Session 2), after the restart that apocalypse-prep-restart.vrs set up (goal at G*,
# 200 m beyond hotspot 1, march at 0.5 m/s, horde 2's front held far from the goal). The boot log holds "boot marker
# sweep: <n> found, <n> queued" and "event apo-test resumed after restart (horde 2/2, <u> units to rebuild)" (checked on
# the log copy). In game: tracked units back to exactly u within 5 min, horde 2's front at or past its saved % (it may
# have marched while nobody was connected), held again once Chaos stands on it (D6: within 60 m of the front, more than
# 90 m from the goal), and the final scoreboard holding the kills from before the restart plus the one here. Then the
# fixture goal and speed are set back, and a second run is started and purged; the orchestrator restarts the server once
# more: that boot logs no resume ("resumed after restart" absent, state.json without "Apocalypse") and `.nyar status`
# reads 0 tracked, read by hand after that boot.
# Run: --var UNITS=<u from the resume line> --var PREP_PCT=<PREP_PCT from prep> --var KILLS_BEFORE=<KILLS_BEFORE from prep>
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
# tracked units back to exactly u (the whole number, so 12 does not pass for 120); the rebuild runs through the spawn
# queue during the boot, so a minute after joining it is done
wait 60
chat .nyar status
expect-log \] tracked units: (?P<TRACKED>[0-9]+) \( timeout=10
expect-calc ${TRACKED} == ${UNITS}
# horde 2's front continues from its saved progress
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] )horde 2 front at (?P<F2X>-?[0-9]+) (?P<F2Z>-?[0-9]+), (?P<F2P>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${F2P} >= ${PREP_PCT}
shot chat apo-boot2-info
chat .devtp ${F2X} ${F2Z}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
# held again: its % does not change in 20 s
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] )horde 2 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<PA>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
wait 20
chat .nyar event info apo-test
expect-log (^|\] )horde 2 front at -?[0-9]+ -?[0-9]+, (?P<PB>[0-9]+) % timeout=10
expect-calc ${PB} == ${PA}
# one rebuilt horde unit killed, then the stop: the scoreboard holds the kills from before the restart and this one
chat .devkill -1967480038 120 1
expect-log \[DEV KILL\] n=(?P<K6>[0-9]+) timeout=10
expect-calc ${K6} == 1
mark
chat .nyar event stop apo-test
expect-log event apo-test stopped
expect-log event apo-test scoreboard: 1 players, (?P<KILLS>[0-9]+) kills timeout=10
expect-calc ${KILLS} >= ${KILLS_BEFORE} + 1
expect-chat Apocalypse test scoreboard timeout=20
shot chat apo-boot2-scoreboard
wait 30
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 ( timeout=40
# the fixture goal and speed back
chat .devtp -1188 -1334
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.goal here
expect-reply apo-test action.goal =
chat .nyar event set apo-test action.marchSpeed 3.0
expect-reply apo-test action.marchSpeed =
# second half (D28): start apo-test again, purge at once, then the orchestrator restarts the server; after that boot
# `.nyar status` must read "tracked units: 0" and the boot log must not hold "apo-test resumed after restart"
mark
chat .nyar event start apo-test
expect-log event apo-test started by Manual timeout=20
expect-log apocalypse apo-test roamers: \+3 at hotspot 1 timeout=30
chat .nyar purge
wait 2
chat .nyar purge confirm
expect-log purge: 1 events ended, [0-9]+ units queued
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 ( timeout=40
console TPHome
